Z||000009||stimpy||02-21-2000||07:51 PM||||Yep, that is the original paint.  It <BR>has endured a whole lot of buffing <BR>and waxing to keep up a shine. (I <BR>love that reflection off of the deck <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) As far as the bolt holes go, <BR>alas, no, not the same as the <BR>spoiler. It has a whole bunch of <BR>little ones. Would be quite a pain <BR>filling them if I ever decided to <BR>remove it. If I did remove it, I <BR>wouldn't put a spoiler on anyway. Not <BR>to knock the cars tha have them, but <BR>they destroy the rear visibility and <BR>IMO they clutter up the lines. My <BR>opinion only...does not reflect the <BR>opinion of this forum, it's members <BR>or the makers of WebTV.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||02-21-2000||08:01 PM||||Phew! I thought I had a messed up plenum! Good to know its not the only one.  never noticed that hole when the engine was red.  Thought I powdercoated a messed up unit. bhooper, thanks for the warm fuzzies on the engine, can't take credit for anythin but paying for it.  Had it done by a very good shop here in OK. <BR>Used all forged bits and pieces, it should hold up to that turbo I got my eye on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. (Once the warranty goes out- heheheh) Of course subject to the approval of the future Mrs stimpy. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
